# Mobile (Flutter) Standards

## Stack

- **Flutter** (Dart) for Android and iOS
- **State management**: BLoC pattern via `flutter_bloc` and `equatable` for states/events
- **Architecture**: Clean Architecture — `presentation` (widgets + BLoC), `domain` (entities, use cases, repository interfaces), `data` (repository implementations, Firebase datasources; see [Firebase Standards](./firebase-standards.mdc))

## Layer rules

| Layer | Contains | May depend on |
|-------|----------|---------------|
| `presentation` | Pages, widgets, `*Bloc`, `*Event`, `*State` | `domain`, Flutter SDK |
| `domain` | Entities, use cases, abstract repositories | Nothing from Flutter/Firebase |
| `data` | Repository impls, mappers, Firebase datasources | `domain`, Firebase SDK |

- Data models / Firestore mappers: use **`flutter-implement-json-serialization`** for `fromJson` / `toJson` on `Map<String, dynamic>` (not HTTP APIs).
- Inject dependencies via constructor or `get_it` / `Provider` at the app root; BLoCs receive use cases, not datasources directly.
- One feature ≈ one folder under `lib/features/<feature>/` with `presentation/`, `domain/`, `data/` subfolders.

## Project skills (mandatory)

Installed skills live in **[`.agents/skills/`](../../.agents/skills/)**. Before starting a related task, **read the matching `SKILL.md` in full** and follow its workflow. Adapt skill output to this project: **BLoC** (not ViewModel/`ChangeNotifier`), **Clean Architecture** layers, and **Firebase SDK** (no HTTP client for app data).

| Task | Skill | Path |
|------|-------|------|
| Feature structure, layers, refactoring for scale | `flutter-apply-architecture-best-practices` | [`.agents/skills/flutter-apply-architecture-best-practices/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/flutter-apply-architecture-best-practices/SKILL.md) |
| Unit tests (use cases, mappers, pure Dart) | `dart-add-unit-test` | [`.agents/skills/dart-add-unit-test/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/dart-add-unit-test/SKILL.md) |
| Integration / E2E tests | `flutter-add-integration-test` | [`.agents/skills/flutter-add-integration-test/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/flutter-add-integration-test/SKILL.md) |
| Mocks for repositories, datasources, use cases | `dart-generate-test-mocks` | [`.agents/skills/dart-generate-test-mocks/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/dart-generate-test-mocks/SKILL.md) |
| JSON / map serialization on data models | `flutter-implement-json-serialization` | [`.agents/skills/flutter-implement-json-serialization/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/flutter-implement-json-serialization/SKILL.md) |
| Declarative routing and deep links | `flutter-setup-declarative-routing` | [`.agents/skills/flutter-setup-declarative-routing/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/flutter-setup-declarative-routing/SKILL.md) |

**When to invoke each skill**

- **Architecture** — new feature folders, layer boundaries, refactoring `lib/` layout.
- **Unit tests** — any new domain logic, mappers, or repository behavior (TDD: failing test first).
- **Integration tests** — user flows spanning screens; prefer Firebase Emulator Suite for Firestore/Auth.
- **Test mocks** — whenever a test doubles a repository interface or Firebase datasource; use with `bloc_test` for BLoC tests.
- **JSON serialization** — `fromJson` / `toJson` (or Firestore `Map<String, dynamic>` mappers) on models in `data/models/`; not for REST endpoints.
- **Declarative routing** — adding routes, `go_router`, deep links, or nested navigation shells.

Other skills under `.agents/skills/` may be used when relevant; the six above are **required** for their matching task types.


- File naming: `<feature>_bloc.dart`, `<feature>_event.dart`, `<feature>_state.dart`
- Events and states are immutable (`equatable` or `freezed`)
- Side effects (navigation, snackbars) via `BlocListener`; UI rebuilds via `BlocBuilder` / `BlocSelector`
- Test with `bloc_test`: `when` → `expect` sequences; mock use cases/repositories, not Firebase

## UI and platform

- Navigation: use **`flutter-setup-declarative-routing`** when adding or changing routes (`go_router`, deep links)
- Prefer `Material` or `Cupertino` per platform guidelines; support light/dark where required
- Use `Theme.of(context)` and responsive layouts; avoid hard-coded magic sizes when design tokens exist
- Accessibility: semantic labels, sufficient contrast, focus order for forms
- Platform channels only when Firebase/plugins do not cover the need

## Testing

- **Unit**: use cases, mappers, repository logic (mocked datasources) — follow **`dart-add-unit-test`**; mocks via **`dart-generate-test-mocks`**
- **BLoC**: `bloc_test` + mocked use cases — generate mocks with **`dart-generate-test-mocks`**
- **Widget**: `flutter_test` + `pumpWidget` with `MaterialApp` and test doubles
- **Integration**: **`flutter-add-integration-test`**; run against Firebase Emulator Suite when testing E2E flows with Firestore/Auth

## Code quality

- Run `dart format .` and `flutter analyze` before considering a task done
- Follow `analysis_options.yaml` lints; fix new warnings in touched files
- English identifiers and comments in code (see `base-standards.mdc`)

## Workflow

- Commits and PR descriptions in Spanish; code in English
- Small, reviewable PRs aligned with one feature or layer at a time
